# 3. Supported Runtime Environments

The architecture must not be restricted to system_server.

Support the following environments through independent runtime adapters.

## 3.1 Android Application Runtime

Inspect the current application's accessible runtime.

Features:
- Application environment detection
- Process information
- ClassLoader discovery
- Loaded class inspection where supported
- Reflection
- Object registration and inspection
- Thread monitoring
- Memory diagnostics
- Runtime snapshots

## 3.2 Android System Server Runtime

Provide specialized support for execution inside the actual system_server process.

Features:
- System server environment detection
- Framework class inspection
- System service discovery
- LocalServices discovery where supported
- Binder-related inspection
- Runtime object inspection through registered providers
- ClassLoader analysis
- Thread and memory diagnostics
- Platform-specific adapters

The implementation must verify the actual execution environment using multiple signals.

UID 1000 alone must never be treated as proof of system_server execution.

## 3.3 Android System Service Runtime

Support custom and platform service environments.

Distinguish:
- android.app.Service
- com.android.server.SystemService
- Other service implementations
- Binder service implementations

Do not assume these service types have identical lifecycle or execution characteristics.

## 3.4 Custom Process Runtime

Provide a reusable agent architecture for authorized processes where the SDK is explicitly integrated.

Each process must inspect its own runtime and expose only explicitly permitted information through IPC.

