# 25. Stability and Security Requirements

This project operates in potentially sensitive Android runtime environments.

Follow these requirements strictly:

1. Do not bypass SELinux.
2. Do not bypass Android permission checks.
3. Do not bypass Binder access controls.
4. Do not assume UID 1000 provides unrestricted access.
5. Do not assume hidden APIs are universally accessible.
6. Do not require root, Shizuku, LSPosed, Xposed, or Frida.
7. Do not modify framework state automatically.
8. Do not execute discovered methods automatically.
9. Do not run expensive scans on the main thread.
10. Do not block system_server startup.
11. Use configurable resource limits.
12. Use cancellation where technically possible.
13. Make reflection mutations explicit.
14. Keep operation logs.
15. Prevent unbounded object graph traversal.
16. Prevent accidental memory leaks through object references.
17. Clearly report unsupported functionality.
18. Treat all external plugin metadata and query inputs as untrusted data.
19. Avoid collecting unrelated sensitive user data.
20. Make diagnostic exports configurable and privacy-aware.

The tool is intended for authorized debugging, platform development, runtime diagnostics, and security research.

